  "hard_rules": [
    "service is the only multi-owner orchestrator and apps depend on service only",
    "symbolic current resolves only at the service boundary and exact requests never reread current",
    "independent owners are not presented as one distributed atomic current snapshot",
    "exact shard and lineage catalog lookup never selects newest first last or nearest",
    "missing search shards never trigger implicit indexing",
    "search lane ranking miss and explanation algorithms remain owned by wow-search",
    "top one sole or highest-band candidate is never selected automatically",
    "search selection requires exact result candidate and digest guards and produces a nonauthority receipt",
    "search_context passes an exact entity root to the existing E3-C context path",
    "project reference search and review lineage producer partitions remain separate",
    "search-derived lineage evidence remains Candidate",
    "review authorization and graph semantic validation are independent",
    "GitHub OS CLI or file identity is not review authorization",
    "review application publishes a new immutable lineage snapshot and never mutates the base",
    "service never raises proof confidence or negative authority",
    "same lineage never implies replacement or migration compatibility",
    "migration artifacts are advisory and never applied",
    "static impact paths never become runtime breakage severity performance taint combat Secret or fixability claims",
    "reason paths never become direct edges",
    "continuation reopens exact retained artifacts and uses cumulative budgets",
    "build and review writes use exact operation ID plus request digest and response-loss recovery",
    "no public success before mandatory resource closure",
    "privacy license consumer and authorization restrictions can only narrow output",
    "no raw SQL FTS storage source filesystem network process editor client model CBM or tool authorization",
    "missing implementations probes corpora benchmarks reviews or checksums are blocking and never pass",
    "no Cargo Rust source or CI during documentation phase"
  ],
